course: dictionary
lesson: 4802
title: Humility, a quality that shows
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humility is a quality, a part of how a person behaves. A humble person does not think they are better or more important than others. «Christians believe God sees what is done in secret and values honesty and humility, so a good player wins without boasting, loses without sulking, and would rather lose fairly than win by cheating.» The clues are wins without boasting and loses without sulking. Humility means not showing off and not acting as if you are the best.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. "A humble player wins without showing off" still makes sense, so you have the right idea. A cheat wants to look better than everyone else, so a cheat is not humble.
explain: The second example uses Scots: «Ye might fool the ref, but ye'll no fool yersel» means you can trick other people, but you cannot trick yourself. Then the text quotes «In humility value others above yourselves» (Philippians 2:3), which tells us humility means putting other people first.
fact: Humility means the quality of being humble: not thinking you are better or more important than others.
fact: In church teaching, humility is a virtue that Christians value, following Jesus, who washed his disciples' feet.
fact: Humility is an uncountable noun, so you do not say "a humility".
fact: Useful phrases: show humility, with humility, and a lesson in humility.
fact: Boasting is the opposite of humility: boasting means showing off how good you are.
exercise: «Christians believe God values honesty and humility.» What does humility mean? | Being very loud | *Thinking you are better than others | Winning every game | Not thinking you are better than others
exercise: A good player «wins without boasting». What does a humble player do after winning? | Cheats next time to win again | Sulks for a week | *Stays modest and does not show off | Tells everyone they are the best
exercise: Which of these is a humble thing to do? | *Admit a mistake and say sorry | Tell everyone you are the best | Cheat to win the game | Refuse to share your toys
test: Jesus washed his disciples' feet. Which quality does this story show? | *Humility | Speed | Cheating | Pride
test: The Scots line says «ye'll no fool yersel». What does it mean? | *You cannot trick yourself | Playing is always fun | The ref is very fair | Everyone can be tricked
exam: Which sentence uses the phrase "with humility" correctly? | They cheated with humility | The winner ran off without a word | He boasted with humility about his score | *She accepted the prize with humility and thanked her team
